"""
The programme rambo: an OpenID provider for a fixed set of first-party
tools, and the commands that manage it.

    rambo serve
    rambo account add alice@example.org --name Alice
    rambo client add --id lucy --kind web --redirect https://lucy.example.org/cb
    rambo keys rotate

serve runs the provider, as FastCGI on a socket in socket_dir behind
Hiawatha or as HTTP on a loopback address for development.  Every other
command manages it from the shell and runs as the owner of its data, never
as root; each change writes an audit line to the system log.  A refusal is
printed after rambo and a colon on the standard error, and the programme
exits with 1.
"""
module Rambo.Main is
    """
    The command of the arguments.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
